{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":214634,"name":null,"username":"MaxYoung","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/13edae/{size}.png","created_at":"2023-08-14T15:32:15.410Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-214634-what-im-trying-to-do-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-214634-what-im-trying-to-do-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat I’m trying to do\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor some reasons, I cannot use update function in OB and have to update plugins manually each time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-214634-things-i-have-tried-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-214634-things-i-have-tried-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eThings I have tried\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe way is to copy plugin files which downloaded from GitHub into .obsidian\\plugins folder.  Then re-start OB. The new version plugin will work well when switched on. But there is a problem. The settings of old version plugin disappear. The new version plugin works with default settings. Thus, I have to reset all settings one by one through all updated plugins. It is boring and waste a lot of my time.\u003cbr\u003e\nIf there is any way to keep settings of plugins when updating?\u003cbr\u003e\nI searched through this forum with key word \" update plugins\" but nothing helps.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks in advance.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2023-08-14T15:32:15.410Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":555,"reads":32,"readers_count":31,"score":2771.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":65071,"topic_slug":"how-to-keep-settings-when-updating-plugins-manually","display_username":null,"primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":55231,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/how-to-keep-settings-when-updating-plugins-manually/65071/1","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":214723,"name":"","username":"CawlinTeffid","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.obsidian.md/cawlinteffid/{size}/82899_2.png","created_at":"2023-08-15T00:11:49.903Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI think plugins’ settings are saved in \u003ccode\u003e.obsidian/plugins/example/data.json\u003c/code\u003e (“.obsidian” being a hidden folder in the root of your vault and “example” being a version of the plugin’s name). So you could try saving a copy of that file elsewhere before updating the plugin and then copying it back afterward.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOr maybe remove “data.json” from the new version of the plugin before installing it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou probably need to restart Obsidian after that (I imagine you’re already doing that).\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2023-08-15T00:13:35.662Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":30,"readers_count":29,"score":31.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":65071,"topic_slug":"how-to-keep-settings-when-updating-plugins-manually","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":false,"staff":true,"user_id":19705,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/how-to-keep-settings-when-updating-plugins-manually/65071/2","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":215409,"name":null,"username":"MaxYoung","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/13edae/{size}.png","created_at":"2023-08-17T14:56:54.786Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003ethank you for ur advice.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut unfortunately, there is no /example folder nor  data.jason file in my .obsidian/plugins folder.\u003cbr\u003e\nI use Win10+OB1.3.7\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2023-08-17T14:56:54.786Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":25,"readers_count":24,"score":10.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":65071,"topic_slug":"how-to-keep-settings-when-updating-plugins-manually","display_username":null,"primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":19705,"username":"CawlinTeffid","name":"","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.obsidian.md/cawlinteffid/{size}/82899_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":55231,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/how-to-keep-settings-when-updating-plugins-manually/65071/3","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":215436,"name":"","username":"CawlinTeffid","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.obsidian.md/cawlinteffid/{size}/82899_2.png","created_at":"2023-08-17T17:17:31.588Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e“Example” is an \u003cem\u003eexample\u003c/em\u003e name. Replace it with the name of the plugin (it may differ a little from the published name). The data.json file will be in \u003cem\u003ethat\u003c/em\u003e folder, not in the plugins folder. Each plugin has one.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2023-08-17T17:17:31.588Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":3,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":20,"readers_count":19,"score":14.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":65071,"topic_slug":"how-to-keep-settings-when-updating-plugins-manually","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":55231,"username":"MaxYoung","name":null,"avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/13edae/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":false,"staff":true,"user_id":19705,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/how-to-keep-settings-when-updating-plugins-manually/65071/4","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":215459,"name":"","username":"gino_m","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/3ec8ea/{size}.png","created_at":"2023-08-17T19:22:35.262Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"CawlinTeffid\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"65071\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forum.obsidian.md/user_avatar/forum.obsidian.md/cawlinteffid/48/82899_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e CawlinTeffid:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou probably need to restart Obsidian after that (I imagine you’re already doing that).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOff topic (sort of):\u003cbr\u003e\nWhat I do when e.g. editing a data.json file (of Editing Toolbar or Apply Patterns plugin, for instance) while Obsidian running is disable and re-enable the plugin using BRAT.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2023-08-17T19:23:13.237Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":4,"reads":16,"readers_count":15,"score":23.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":65071,"topic_slug":"how-to-keep-settings-when-updating-plugins-manually","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":58049,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"user_suspended":true,"post_url":"/t/how-to-keep-settings-when-updating-plugins-manually/65071/5","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":215583,"name":null,"username":"MaxYoung","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/13edae/{size}.png","created_at":"2023-08-18T13:30:51.103Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eunderstood. thank you. i will try it next time.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2023-08-18T13:30:51.103Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":4,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":14,"readers_count":13,"score":2.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":65071,"